  "notes": "COMPOUND VERB:\n{住|す}む (to live) + {慣|な}れる (to become accustomed)\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {住|す}み{慣|な}れた{場所|ばしょ} - a place one is used to living\n- {住|す}み{慣|な}れた{町|まち} - a town one is comfortable in\n- {住|す}み{慣|な}れた{家|いえ} - a home one is accustomed to\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n~{慣|な}れる compound verbs (become used to ~):\n- {聞|き}き{慣|な}れる - become used to hearing\n- {食|た}べ{慣|な}れる - become used to eating\n- {見慣|みな}れる - become used to seeing\n- {使|つか}い{慣|な}れる - become used to using",
